/		SOURCE FILE CONFORMED TO OFFICIAL PDP-8 SOURCE CODE CONVENTIONS, AS
/		MANDATED BY P?S SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT POLICIES AND PROCEDURES DICTATED
/		PERSONALLY BY MARIO DENOBILI CIRCA 1968.

/		[NOTE: MEMBERS OF THE WILLIAM CLAUDE FIELDS MEMORIAL PROGRAMMING GROUP
/		(WCFMPG) HAVE BEEN KNOWN TO USE THE "\" CHARACTER WHERE MOST
/		CONTEMPORANEOUS COMPUTER PROFESSIONALS WOULD EMPLOY THE "/" CHARACTER
/		WITHIN PROGRAMS DESIGNED FOR DEC SYSTEMS.  IT IS THEORIZED THIS VARIANCE
/		DERIVES FROM THE PERSONAL EXPERIENCE OF THE MEMBERS, ALL OF WHOM HAD
/		CONTACT WITH VARIOUS IBM PRODUCTS WHERE THIS IS COMMON PRACTICE.]

/		[NOTE: MEMBERS OF THE POLY QUESTION SOCIETY (P?S) GENERALLY DO NOT
/		SUPPORT THIS EARLIER CONVENTION ON DEC SYSTEMS.  AS SUCH, THE REST OF
/		THIS DOCUMENT WILL REFER TO PDP-8 MODELS AND OTHER DEFINITIONS USING THE
/		"/" CHARACTER, AS IS CUSTOMARY THROUGHOUT ALL PROGRAMS DESIGNED FOR THE
/		PDP-8 COMPUTER ARCHITECTURE.]

/		LAST EDIT: 22-MAR-2014 CJL

/		THIS SOURCE CODE FILE IS A COMBINATION OF LAB-8/E BASIC AND 8K BASIC FOR
/		THE PDP-8.  TO CREATE THE LAB-8/E EDITION, SET "MACHINE=1"; TO CREATE
/		THE 8K PDP-8 EDITION, SET "MACHINE=0".  [NOTE: "MACHINE=0" IS THE
/		DEFAULT SETTING; SEE BELOW FOR ADDITIONAL ASSEMBLY PARAMETERS.]

/		THIS IS THE ORIGINAL 8K BASIC [AND LAB-8/E BASIC] DESIGNED FOR USE WITH
/		PAPER-TAPE SOFTWARE LOADERS [RIM AND BIN] ONLY.  SQUEEZING EVERY LAST
/		BIT OF AVAILABLE MEMORY SPACE IS A DESIGN GOAL.  AS A RESULT, THERE ARE
/		DIFFICULTIES ASSOCIATED WITH LOADING THIS PROGRAM FROM PREVAILING PDP-8
/		STORAGE-BASED OPERATING SYSTEMS, ALL OF WHICH REQUIRE A SOMEWHAT LARGER
/		AND/OR DIFFERENT RESERVED AREA FROM THE PREVAILING PAPER-TAPE LOADERS.
/	DEFAULT GLOBAL SETTINGS.

/	PARAMETERS ARE PROVIDED TO MODIFY THE BINARY OUTPUT OF THIS ASSEMBLY FOR A
/	VARIETY OF PURPOSES INCLUDING BUG FIXES, ALTERNATE MEMORY CONFIGURATIONS AND
/	BINARY COMPATIBILITY TESTING IN CONJUNCTION WITH AN EXTERNAL TESTING PROGRAM.
/	DEFAULT VALUES WILL PRODUCE THE STANDARD RELEASE OF THE ORIGINAL 8K BASIC.

	IFNDEF	MACHINE	<MACHINE=0>	/THE DEFAULT SETTING CREATES THE 8K VERSION.
					/CHANGE TO "MACHINE=1" FOR THE LAB-8/E VERSION.

	IFNDEF	DEB4K	<DEB4K=	0>	/THE DEFAULT SETTING CREATES THE ORIGINAL
					/RELEASE WHICH IS INCOMPATIBLE WITH ALL SOFTWARE
					/DEBUGGERS.  SETTING "DEB4K= 1" WILL FREE
					/LOCATION 00004 AS THE BASIS FOR SOFTWARE
					/DEBUGGING OF NON-INTERRUPT CODE LOADED INTO
					/FIELD 0; BINARY COMPATIBILITY WITH THE ORIGINAL
					/RELEASE WILL BE LOST.

	IFNDEF	DEB8K	<DEB8K=	0>	/THE DEFAULT SETTING CREATES THE ORIGINAL
					/RELEASE WHICH IS INCOMPATIBLE WITH ALL SOFTWARE
					/DEBUGGERS.  SETTING "DEB8K= 1" WILL FREE
					/LOCATION 10004 AS THE BASIS FOR SOFTWARE
					/DEBUGGING OF NON-INTERRUPT CODE LOADED INTO
					/FIELD 1; BINARY COMPATIBILITY WITH THE ORIGINAL
					/WILL BE LOST; SETTING "DEB4K= 1" MIGHT ALSO BE
					/REQUIRED SINCE MANY SOFTWARE DEBUGGERS WILL
					/MODIFY LOCATION 00004 WHEN EXTENDED MEMORY
					/BREAKPOINTS ARE IN EFFECT.  [NOTE: IT IS NOT
					/NECESSARY TO CHANGE THIS SETTING UNLESS ACTUAL
					/EXTENDED MEMORY BREAKPOINTS ARE CONTEMPLATED;
					/MANY DEBUGGING SESSIONS ONLY REQUIRE FIELD 0
					/BREAKPOINTS.]

	IFNDEF	MFLD	<MFLD=	0>	/THE DEFAULT SETTING ALLOWS PROGRAM EXECUTION IN
					/FIELD 0.  TO ALLOW BINARY COMPATIBILITY TESTING
					/USE "MFLD= 5" WHICH IS INCOMPATIBLE WITH NORMAL
					/EXECUTION.  A SPECIAL TESTING PROGRAM CAN BE
					/USED TO COMPARE FIELD 5 TO FIELD 3 AND COMPARE
					/FIELD 6 TO FIELD 4.  [NOTE: THESE PARAMETERS
					/CAN BE ADJUSTED DEPENDING ON SPECIFIC OPERATING
					/SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS.  CORRESPONDING CHANGES
					/MUST ALSO BE MADE TO THE TESTING PROGRAM.]

	IFNDEF	XFLD	<XFLD=	1>	/BY DEFAULT, THE EXTENDED MEMORY PORTION OF THE
					/PROGRAM IS LOADED INTO FIELD 1.  TO ALLOW
					/BINARY COMPATIBILITY TESTING, USE "XFLD= 6"
					/WHILE MAINTAINING THE DEFAULT SETTING OF
					/"XEQFL1= 1" AS DESCRIBED BELOW.  TO CHANGE
					/BINARY PROGRAM LOADING TO A HIGHER FIELD, SET
					/BOTH "XFLD" AND "XEQFL1" TO THE SAME HIGHER
					/VALUE [UP TO 7].  THIS MAY BE REQUIRED TO ALLOW
					/PROPER LOADING AND FUNCTIONALITY WHEN EXECUTION
					/IS INITIATED UNDER CERTAIN OPERATING SYSTEMS.
	IFNDEF	XEQFL0	<XEQFL0=0>	/BY DEFAULT, THE CODE MEANT FOR FIELD 0
					/ASSEMBLES FOR USE IN FIELD 0 REGARDLESS OF
					/ACTUAL LOADING FIELD AS DETERMINED BY "MFLD".
					/GENERALLY, THIS SETTING SHOULD NOT BE CHANGED
					/AS THE RESULTANT BINARY PROGRAM WOULD BE
					/NONFUNCTIONAL DUE TO THE HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS
					/OF INTERRUPT HANDLING IN FIELD 0.  "XEQFL0" IS
					/USED AS A SYMBOLIC REFERENCE IN FIELD CHANGE
					/INSTRUCTIONS TO DISTINGUISH EXTENDED MEMORY
					/REFERENCES FROM LOADING DIRECTIVES AS USED
					/ELSEWHERE.

	IFNDEF	XEQFL1	<XEQFL1=1>	/BY DEFAULT, THE CODE NORMALLY INTENDED TO
					/EXECUTE IN FIELD 1 ASSEMBLES FOR FIELD 1 USAGE
					/[REGARDLESS OF WHERE THE CODE IS ACTUALLY LOADED
					/AS DETERMINED BY "XFLD"].  THIS PARAMETER SHOULD
					/BE CHANGED TO MATCH THE SETTING OF "XFLD" TO
					/PRODUCE A WORKING VERSION INTENDED TO LOAD INTO
					/A DIFFERENT EXTENDED MEMORY FIELD.  DO NOT
					/CHANGE "XEQFL1" WHEN CHANGING "XFLD" IF TESTING
					/FOR BINARY COMPATIBILITY [WHICH CONFLICTS WITH
					/NORMAL EXECUTION].

	IFNDEF	HIDCON	<HIDCON=0>	/BY DEFAULT UNASSEMBLED CONDITIONAL CODE FOR THE
					/PROGRAM VERSION NOT IN EFFECT IS DISPLAYED AS
					/IGNORED TEXT.  SETTING "HIDCON=1 WILL INHIBIT
					/LISTING OF THE UNASSEMBLED CONDITIONAL CODE.

	IFNDEF	OFF	<OFF=	1>	/IF "HIDCON=1" THIS WILL BE USED TO TURN OFF
					/DISPLAY OF UNASSEMBLED CONDITIONAL CODE.

	IFNDEF	ON	<ON=	0>	/IF "HIDCON=1" THIS WILL BE USED TO TURN ON
					/DISPLAY OF UNASSEMBLED CONDITIONAL CODE.


	IFNDEF	LPTFIX	<LPTFIX=0>	/THE ORIGINAL VERSIONS HAVE A LINEPRINTER STATUS
					/BUG WITH REGARD TO HANDLING THE ERROR FLAG
					/WHICH CAN RAISE ON VARIOUS SPECIFIC HARDWARE
					/VARIANTS OF THE DEVICE 66 STANDARD LINEPRINTER.
					/DEPENDING ON THE CURRENT ONLINE STATUS, THE
					/ERROR FLAG CAN MAKE EITHER VERSION OF BASIC
					/UNUSABLE.  BY DEFAULT, THE CODE ASSEMBLES WITH
					/THIS PROGRAMMING BUG PRESENT.  SET "LPTFIX= 1"
					/TO PRODUCE A FULLY FUNCTIONAL PROGRAM AT THE
					/EXPENSE OF BINARY COMPATIBILITY WITH PREVAILING
					/DOCUMENTATION.

/	ADDITIONAL GLOBAL SETTINGS MAY BE ADDED AS NECESSARY.
/	BINARY COMPATIBILITY ISSUES.

/	THE SOURCE CODING FOR THIS PROGRAM IS THE RESULT OF AN ONGOING RESTORATION
/	PROJECT BY SEVERAL PDP-8 EXPERTS AND ENTHUSIASTS FOR THE PURPOSE OF
/	DOCUMENTING THIS HISTORICALLY IMPORTANT PDP-8 PROGRAM.  TO ENSURE BINARY
/	COMPATIBILITY, A TESTING PROGRAM HAS BEEN WRITTEN BY CHARLES LASNER TO
/	CONFIRM THE SOURCE CODE COMPLETELY MATCHES AVAILABLE BINARY FILES DERIVED FROM
/	SURVIVING PAPER TAPES IN STANDARD BIN FORMAT.

/	DUE TO SPECIFIC LOGISTIC ISSUES OF THIS PROGRAM, IT IS NECESSARY TO LOAD THE
/	PROGRAM INTO MEMORY FIELDS NOT RELATED TO THE NORMAL INTENDED OPERATION.  AS
/	SUCH, VARIOUS PARAMETERS MUST BE SET TO SPECIFIC NONSTANDARD VALUES FOR USE
/	WITH THE TESTING PROGRAM.

/	TO PRODUCE CUSTOMIZED BINARY OUTPUT FOR USE WITH THE COMPATIBILITY TEST
/	PROGRAM, ENABLE TESTING BELOW.  FOR NORMAL USAGE, DISABLE THE TESTING
/	DEFINITIONS.

	MFLD=	5			/LOAD THE FIELD 0 CODE INTO FIELD 5.
	XFLD=	6			/LOAD THE FIELD 1 CODE INTO FIELD 6.

/	NOTE: DURING TESTING, FIELD 3 WILL BE LOADED WITH THE ORIGINAL RELEASED BINARY
/	PROGRAM FIELD 0 CONTENTS.  ADDITIONALLY, FIELD 4 WILL BE LOADED WITH THE
/	ORIGINAL RELEASED BINARY PROGRAM FIELD 1 CONTENTS.  THE CONTENTS OF FIELD 3
/	WILL BE COMPARED TO THE CONTENTS OF FIELD 5; SIMILARLY, THE CONTENTS OF FIELD
/	4 WILL BE COMPARED TO THE CONTENTS OF FIELD 6.  THE TESTING PROGRAM WILL
/	INDICATE ANY DISCREPANCIES BETWEEN THE ORIGINAL RELEASED BINARY AND THE BINARY
/	OUTPUT OF THE ASSEMBLY OF THIS FILE.  [NOTE: ALL UNUSED LOCATIONS IN ALL
/	TESTED FIELDS WILL BE PRELOADED WITH 0000 TO PREVENT FALSE POSITIVE RESULTS.]
/	[NOTE: MODIFIED VERSIONS OF THE ORIGINAL RELEASED BINARY FILES THAT LOAD INTO
/	FIELDS 3 AND 4 ARE AVAILABLE FROM CHARLES LASNER FOR USE WITH THE BINARY
/	COMPATIBILITY TESTING PROGRAM.]

/	THE TESTING PROGRAM LOADS INTO FIELD 0 AND STARTS AT THE STANDARD ADDRESS OF
/	00200.  OVERALL LOADING PARAMETERS WERE CHOSEN FOR MAXIMUM COMPATIBILITY WITH
/	THE OS/8 AND P?S/8 OPERATING SYSTEMS; ALL KNOWN LOADING RESTRICTIONS OF BOTH
/	OPERATING SYSTEMS ARE AVOIDED.  CONTACT CHARLES LASNER IF THERE IS FURTHER
/	INTEREST IN THIS FAIRLY TRIVIAL MULTIPLE-FIELD COMPARISON PROGRAM.

/	ONCE THE TWO MAIN PROGRAM VARIANTS [8K BASIC USING "MACHINE=0" AND LAB-/E
/	BASIC USING "MACHINE=1"] HAVE BEEN CONFIRMED, ALL BINARY COMPATIBILITY TESTING
/	PARAMETERS MAY BE RESET OR REMOVED FROM THIS SOURCE FILE.

/	DECLARED GLOBAL SETTINGS.

/	HIDCON=	1			/DO NOT DISPLAY UNASSEMBLED CONDITIONAL CODE.
	MACHINE=0			/CREATE 8K VERSION.

/	DEPENDENT DEFINITIONS.

	CODFLD=	XEQFL0^10		/MAIN CODE FIELD FOR FIELD CHANGE INSTRUCTIONS.
	DATFLD=	XEQFL1^10		/MAIN DATA FIELD FOR FIELD CHANGE INSTRUCTIONS.
	XLIST	OFF			/TURN LISTING OFF.
	IFNZRO	HIDCON-1!MACHINE	<XLIST	ON>
	IFNZRO	MACHINE			<

/	THE FOLLOWING CODE IS USED IN THE LAB-8/E BASIC VERSION TO MAKE THE PROGRAM
/	SELF-STARTING.  PAPER-TAPE CHECKSUMMING CONVENTIONS ARE PROPERLY ADHERED TO.
/	[NOTE: THIS ASSUMES THE MAY 10, 1967 RELEASE OF THE BIN LOADER, DEC-08-LBAA,
/	IS PERFORMING THE PROGRAM LOAD; NOT ALL VERSIONS OF THE BIN LOADER CONFORM TO
/	THIS CONVENTION.]

/	THE LAB-8/E VERSION OF BASIC MUST BE LOADED BY THE BIN LOADER IN FIELD 1 SINCE
/	THE PROGRAM LOADS OVER MOST OF THE LAST PAGE OF FIELD 0.  THE BIN LOADER CAN
/	BE LOADED BY THE RIM LOADER IN FIELD 1; LAB-8/E BASIC ONLY RESERVES THE SPACE
/	REQUIRED BY THE RIM LOADER; THIS ALLOWS THE BIN LOADER TO BE RELOADED AS
/	NECESSARY.  NOTE: THE LAB-8/E VERSION IS INCOMPATIBLE WITH ALL STORAGE-BASED
/	PDP-8 OPERATING SYSTEMS.

	FIELD	XFLD			/THIS IS WHERE THE BIN LOADER SHOULD BE LOADED.

	M376=	7700			/WHERE THE NORMAL BINARY LOADER EXIT
					/"HLT" INSTRUCTION IS LOADED.

	*M376				/OVER THE BINARY LOADER CODE EXIT ROUTINE.

	JMP I	UGETWD/[6000]		/JUST GO START OUR PROGRAM DIRECTLY.

	*6000				/ONCE-ONLY CODE CAN RUN FROM HERE.

	DCA	UTEMP			/SAVE THE CHECKSUM.
	TAD	INTHLT/(HLT)		/GET A "HLT" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	INTPLC/(M376)		/RESTORE THE BINARY LOADER TO NORMAL.
	TAD	UTEMP			/GET THE CHECKSUM.
	SZA				/SKIP IF LOAD OK.
	JMP I	INTPLC			/GOTO NORMAL "HLT" LOCATION WITH BAD CHECKSUM.
	CIF CDF	CODFLD			/WE STARTUP IN FIELD 0.
	JMP I	.+1/(START)		/GO START IT UP.
	START				/THROUGH HERE.

INTHLT,	HLT				/CONSTANT 7402.
INTPLC,	M376				/ADDRESS OF OVERLAYED BIN LOADER CODE.

					>
	XLIST	OFF			/TURN LISTING OFF AFTER CONDITIONAL SECTION.

/	CONDITIONAL ALTERNATIVES [IF ANY] GO HERE.

	XLIST	ON			/TURN LISTING BACK ON AFTER ALL CONDITIONALS.
/	BASIC4.52

/	MOST OF THIS CODE IS BASED ON 4K BASIC.

	FIELD	MFLD			/TO HELP BINARY LOADER IN CASE HE BLOWS IT.

/	NUMERIC LOAD DEFINITIONS.

/	USE VALUES KNOWN TO WORK ON THE ORIGINAL PDP-8 AND NEWER MODELS ONLY.  NOTE:
/	THIS PROGRAM IS INCOMPATIBLE WITH THE PDP-5 AND PDP-8/S.

	NL0001=	CLA IAC			/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 0001.
	NL0002=	CLA CLL CML RTL		/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 0002.
	NL2000=	CLA CLL CML RTR		/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 2000.
	NL4000=	CLA CLL CML RAR		/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 4000.
	NL7775=	CLA CLL CMA RTL		/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 7775.
	NL7776=	CLA CLL CMA RAL		/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 7776.
	NL7777=	CLA CMA			/LOAD ACCUMULATOR WITH 7777.

